{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/525739-durance-in-currently-run-chronicle","id":525739,"title":"Durance in currently run chronicle","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-05-23T11:48:55-07:00","id":525739,"title":"Durance in currently run chronicle","content":"i have mortal PCs in mine <b>Changeling</b> game I run. Of course, players want to make characters in to proper fea rather soon. Questions are for setting consitancy - <b>What are the shortes Durances, in Earth time perspective?</b> Are some good advices on running mortal-to-changeling character in game? How would you handle this kind situation?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-24T02:23:56-07:00","id":526475,"title":"","content":"Minutes. Seconds even. It's not an uncommon fae trope. The inversion to the &quot;gone for what felt like a moment, returns to find decades have passed&quot; is &quot;endure decades away from the world, return aged from decades apart to find no one has even noticed they have gone&quot;.<br /> <br /> Pretty easy to slot into a game, although you might want to talk to your players regarding how they feel regarding the the durance itself and its impact on their characters. On the one hand, letting the GM have total control over the durance they experience reinforces the themes of Changeling beautifully (being helpless, being acted upon, and then the escape), but it's pretty heavy stuff and something you would need to make certain your players are ok with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-24T04:00:03-07:00","id":526523,"title":"","content":"The actual time spent in Arcadia can be whatever is needed. Time there is variable enough that the only basic rule is that there can't be backwards time travel (though they might be made to look like they've de-aged).<br /> <br /> As for how I'd go about it, there would be two main avenues I'd go. The first would be the fetch route. The mortal gets separated from the rest of the group and then is reunited. Talk it over with the mortal player and have them play a fetch for a little while. Probably three or so play sessions. Have them start dropping hints that something is wrong. The character is suddenly different in some way with their personality. Or maybe nothing is wrong and the fetch is completely human-like. If the group doesn't catch on or if there's nothing to catch onto, have the newly escaped Changeling appear and explain the situation.. The group can discuss how to handle the situation from there.<br /> <br /> The other option is to have the mortal captured and the group has to mount a rescue. This can be as complex as assaulting a Hollow castle's dungeon with days of planning or breaking down a door to the Hedge that was locked when it closed. In either case they arrive to find the changeling already transformed and wondering what took the group so long to rescue them. Why didn't they try harder?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2290-trickyboots","name":"TrickyBoots","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2290_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}